WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:07.060
Westworld Season 3 Episode 3 is called “The
Absence of Field”. This refers to a poem

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:12.240
by Mark Strand, about a person who exists
in the absence of something else . Cause in

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:18.079
this episode, the real Charlotte Hale is dead,
but a host Charlotte pretends to be her – she

00:00:18.079 --> 00:00:24.319
exists in Charlotte’s absence, she fills
in the gap that Charlotte left behind.

00:00:24.319 --> 00:00:28.609
The episode starts with a flashback to the
real human Charlotte during the Westworld

00:00:28.609 --> 00:00:34.340
massacre – shortly before we see her in
Season 2. Charlotte is terrified, thinks she’s

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:38.562
gonna die, so she records a message for her
son Nathan – [by talking in to the face

00:00:38.562 --> 00:00:41.190
of a host so it’s stored in memory]. Later,
in Season 2, Dolores killed Charlotte, and

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:46.620
impersonated her in a Charlotte body. Then,
Dolores left Westworld in the Charlotte body,

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:52.390
and brought with her five host brains, or
“pearls”. Out in the real world, she recreated

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:58.289
Bernard from her memories . And she created
this new Charlotte host. This scene actually

00:00:58.289 --> 00:01:03.250
happens before the rest of Season 3 – cause
Dolores has Bernard’s pearl, so this is

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:08.670
before she lets Bernard loose and he becomes
a fugitive . It’s interesting that Bernard’s

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:14.299
pearl is coloured red. Previously, all five
of Dolores’ pearls looked black. Maybe the

00:01:14.299 --> 00:01:19.890
colour changed when Dolores recreated Bernard
– his personality now seems to include aspects

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:25.890
of the human Arnold. When the humans James
Delos and Ford were made into hosts, they

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:31.490
also had red pearls – so the red might indicate
Bernard’s human side.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:36.950
Dolores talks with this new host Charlotte,
who acts almost like a newborn child. She’s

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:43.950
confused at first , but then she remembers
who she is . So – who is she? Presumably,

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:48.610
new Charlotte has one of these five brains
in her head – someone who Dolores took from

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:53.909
Westworld to the real world. Dolores says
she trusts this person , and they know each

00:01:53.909 --> 00:02:00.820
other – they embrace, like how Dolores and
Teddy once embraced. Teddy always was Dolores’

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:06.469
closest ally. So maybe Dolores put his mind
in this Charlotte body. Last season, Dolores

00:02:06.469 --> 00:02:12.500
did say that Teddy is “one last soul to
carry to the new world” . But Dolores uploaded

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:18.230
Teddy to the Sublime, the digital paradise
for hosts. She left him behind, and it was

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:24.050
big emotional moment showing the cost of Dolores’
choices . It seemed like an end to Teddy’s

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:30.380
story – so will they really bring him back?
There are other possibilities. The way Charlotte

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:36.300
acts with a gentle innocence is similar to
how Clementine used to act. Clementine was

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:41.880
lobotomised, then turned into a mindless deathbot
– so she probably can’t be this new Charlotte.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:48.640
But Clementine might be a useful weapon, so
maybe Clem is one of Dolores’ other pearls.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:54.230
Maybe new Charlotte is Peter Abernathy, Dolores’
host father. His brain got all scrambled cause

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:59.750
it held the “encryption key” to the Forge,
Westworld’s data on human minds. Serac wants

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:04.660
that key , so maybe Peter’s brain will be
important again this season. But Dolores had

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:09.251
an emotional farewell with her father before
ripping out his brain – it felt like an

00:03:09.251 --> 00:03:15.090
ending, and he was such a minor character
anyway, so he also probably isn’t Charlotte.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:20.130
Angela worked with Dolores in Season 2. But
Angela blew herself up in the Cradle, specifically

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:26.840
to destroy all the host backups, so she probably
won’t come back. It could be Hector or Armistice

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:31.050
– they are useful fighters. But Dolores
doesn’t really know them – she’s never

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:36.300
spoken to Hector or Armistice. So they can’t
be this new Charlotte, who Dolores knows and

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:40.980
trusts – but maybe Hector and Armistice
could be in these other pearls.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:46.760
So of these five pearls, we know one is Bernard.
Another could be Hector or Armistice or Peter

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:53.460
or Clementine. The one inside Charlotte might
be Teddy, but there could be a different twist.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:58.420
Dolores and new Charlotte are surrounded by
imagery of mirrors and reflection. In their

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:03.580
hotel room, there’s this statue of two identical
figures reflected symmetrically, and this

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:09.450
symmetrical artwork. There’s also a mirror,
and these shadows, there’s copies and reflections

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:15.930
everywhere. Maybe new Charlotte is a copy
of Dolores, and that’s why Dolores trusts

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:22.199
her and knows her – she is her. Dolores
says “No one knows you like I do. No one

00:04:22.199 --> 00:04:28.710
knows me like you” – that line itself
is like a mirror image. New Charlotte says

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:35.110
“Why can't I be myself? Like you?” – which
could mean Charlotte’s real self is Dolores

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:41.770
. Dolores’ goal is the birth of a new host
species , to grow like the cells in the opening

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:48.520
theme – maybe, as a host, she won’t reproduce
sexually, but by self-replication, by copying

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:53.949
herself. Maybe all of these pearls she took
from Westworld are blank, and she’s just

00:04:53.949 --> 00:04:59.389
copying herself onto them. Like the Smiths
in The Matrix, Dolores could fill the world

00:04:59.389 --> 00:05:07.660
with herself. But new Charlotte is not identical
to Dolores – she’s younger and more vulnerable,

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:13.520
she’s more like a daughter than a copy,
and Dolores cares for her like a mother. Their

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:19.860
embrace is like Maeve with her daughter. Motherhood
is a big theme this episode – with Charlotte

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:26.430
and Nathan, Caleb and his mother. And all
these relationships are difficult. Cause kids

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:30.710
aren’t just copies of their parents, they
have their own influences and conflicts that

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:35.919
make them grow into something new. So there
are a million possibilities, but it seems

00:05:35.919 --> 00:05:42.120
likely that new Charlotte is a copy of Dolores.
And thematically, their relationship explores

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:47.999
motherhood, and growth, and change. That’s
how life survives – by never staying the

00:05:47.999 --> 00:05:51.640
same.
Dolores gets new Charlotte to impersonate

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:56.669
the old human Charlotte. Because old Charlotte
worked at Delos, the company that owns the

00:05:56.669 --> 00:06:02.029
Westworld parks, and Dolores wants Delos to
keep making hosts – maybe she just needs

00:06:02.029 --> 00:06:08.430
the pearls to copy herself onto. Charlotte
gets a giant robot – the Delos website calls

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:14.409
this The Mech, it’s apparently a cutting-edge
dystopian riot control machine. Apparently,

00:06:14.409 --> 00:06:19.319
Delos made three hundred of them , and Charlotte
says she’s sure she “can find some use

00:06:19.319 --> 00:06:24.669
for them” , so no doubt she’ll send these
things on a rampage for the robot revolution.

00:06:24.669 --> 00:06:29.159
Charlotte learns that she’s lost control
of the Delos company – cause a heap of stock

00:06:29.159 --> 00:06:32.129
was bought by companies controlled by Serac
.

00:06:32.129 --> 00:06:37.879
A Delos woman called Irene says that Serac
is like a black hole, because he’s invisible

00:06:37.879 --> 00:06:43.310
– there’s no information about him anywhere
. But, like a black hole, you can detect him

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:48.660
by his influence . Serac is the wealthiest
man in the world , but all his wealth his

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:54.849
hidden, so he can be detected in the world’s
missing money, in economic negative space

00:06:54.849 --> 00:07:01.559
– like that poem again, the absence of field
. Irene says that Delos once sold Serac a

00:07:01.559 --> 00:07:06.520
sample of data from the Forge – all the
human minds recorded in the Westworld park.

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:11.560
And that’s why Serac bought out Delos, he
wants that data , which makes sense, because

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:17.039
Serac runs Rehoboam, which uses surveillance
data to predict and control people.

00:07:17.039 --> 00:07:21.500
New Charlotte goes to the home of the old
human Charlotte – she intrudes into the

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:27.510
life of the dead person she’s impersonating.
And she finds old Charlotte’s ex, Jake,

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:32.849
who startles Charlotte so she immediately
starts fucking him out of pure confusion.

00:07:32.849 --> 00:07:39.009
Jake calls Charlotte “Charlie”. And Charlie
is the name of Arnold’s dead son. There

00:07:39.009 --> 00:07:44.360
was a crazy theory years ago that Charlie
is somehow a younger Charlotte. So this line

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:48.550
might be the showrunners’ way of teasing
the audience over this theory – Jonathan

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:51.809
Nolan says they “love to fuck with Reddit”
.

00:07:51.809 --> 00:07:57.229
We meet old Charlotte’s son Nathan, which
forces us to see old Charlotte differently.

00:07:57.229 --> 00:08:02.210
In past seasons, she was always a ruthless
corporate headkicker with zero regard for

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:08.339
human or host life . So it wasn’t terribly
sad when Dolores killed her. But now we see

00:08:08.339 --> 00:08:13.770
that poor Nathan has lost his mother, so we’re
forced to see some tragedy in old Charlotte’s

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:19.370
death. Also, these arrow shapes look a lot
like these shapes on Rehoboam in the intro,

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:24.120
which is.. curious.
New Charlotte mentions that elephants are

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:29.779
now extinct. The only elephants left are these
host elephants in The Raj. It’s like how

00:08:29.779 --> 00:08:34.270
humans might go extinct and be replaced by
hosts – just like how human Charlotte was

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:38.790
replaced by host Charlotte.
We learn that old Charlotte was a pretty shitty

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:44.330
mom to Nathan – Nathan says that Charlotte
doesn’t love him . So new Charlotte does

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:49.280
her best to be a mother to this human child,
just like Dolores tries to be a mother to

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:54.640
new Charlotte. Once again, the most real and
sincere relationships in this series are not

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:59.880
with the humans, they’re with the hosts.
At Delos, Charlotte learns that someone at

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:05.660
Westworld stole some host brains, including
Maeve’s. We saw last episode that Maeve’s

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:10.100
brain was taken – apparently so that Serac
could put Maeve in his simulation, along with

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:16.750
a bunch of other brains. So there’s a mole
at Westworld, working for Serac, stealing

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:22.310
host brains . We later learn that old human
Charlotte was working for Serac, but she’s

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:28.440
not the only mole. Because old Charlotte was
likely dead before Maeve’s brain was stolen.

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:33.621
And Serac says he has other people under his
control , so it sounds like there’s another

00:09:33.621 --> 00:09:38.570
mole at Westworld, who stole Maeve’s brain.
There aren’t many options on who this could

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:43.750
be – cause the only surviving humans who
we know at Westworld are Felix, Sylvester,

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:49.040
David Benioff and D. B. Weiss – so unless
one them works for Serac, the mole must be

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:53.960
a new character – or perhaps some even more
ridiculous twist.

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:59.080
New Charlotte starts cutting herself, she’s
freaking out, feeling like the old human Charlotte

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:05.270
is inside her, trying to cut her way out . New
Charlotte might have some Forge data on old

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:10.990
Charlotte, like a copy of old Charlotte inside
her so she knows how to act like her. But

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:17.190
behaving and thinking like someone is pretty
close to being that person. The whole idea

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:22.540
of hosts in this story is that machines pretending
to be people become those people – like,

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:27.950
Maeve didn’t really have a daughter, she’s
a robot – but she played the role of a mother,

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:34.710
and that made that identity true. So now this
new Charlotte, playing the role of old Charlotte,

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:41.290
is becoming like her – she’s playing her
role “a little too well” . The cutting

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:47.370
is interesting, because when the human James
Delos was made into a host, he also cut himself.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:53.720
The idea is that copied human minds struggle
to survive in host bodies . Also, the cuts

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:59.880
are shaped a bit like these circular images
from Rehoboam, which is… interesting.

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:04.431
Charlotte comes to Dolores for support, and
all the dialogue and imagery fits with the

00:11:04.431 --> 00:11:09.670
idea of new Charlotte being a copy of Dolores
. Dolores says that to take back control of

00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:15.420
Delos, she’ll need to visit “an old friend”
. Dolores has called William an “old friend”

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:17.510
before , [and William twice calls Dolores
“old friend” ]. And William is super rich

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:22.380
and has lots of Delos stock. So maybe Dolores
and Charlotte will get William’s help to

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:27.950
take back Delos from Serac. Last season, there
was a flash-forward to a “far future”

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:32.890
host version of William in a loop . But in
the present timeline, we saw William alive

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:36.900
in Westworld .
New Charlotte sees the recording of old human

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:42.130
Charlotte – it’s a heartfelt message to
her son Nathan. Akecheta once said that you

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:47.910
live “as long as the last person who remembers
you” . Old Charlotte is remembered, and

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:53.590
in some sense she lives on in new Charlotte.
New Charlotte is moved by this message, it

00:11:53.590 --> 00:11:59.320
seems to inspire her to be a mother to Nathan.
She finds Nathan with a creepy child predator

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:03.950
– so Charlotte murders him on the spot.
Then Charlotte takes the man’s dog, and

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:09.740
gives it to Nathan – a dog is not as cool
as an elephant – but it’s a start. Charlotte

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:15.730
makes a real connection with Nathan, and she
achieves it through murder – this is a fierce

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:22.550
kind of motherhood. She says this murder helps
her to remember who she is – a “predator”

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:29.120
. So is she referring to her identity as Dolores,
or her identity as old Charlotte, or as both?

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:34.190
Maybe she’s finding a new identity from
a combination of influences. Cause that’s

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:40.320
how people grow, right? New Charlotte started
like a child, vulnerable and innocent. Then

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:45.310
she went through a teenage stage, rebelling
against her mother Dolores . Now, she moves

00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:50.430
towards adulthood, with new confidence and
certainty in her identity.

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:54.960
New Charlotte tells Nathan “You are my sunshine”
, cause she learned from old Charlotte’s

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:59.760
message that she used to sing that song to
Nathan . And this unlocks a mystery. Cause

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:04.650
throughout the episode, Charlotte gets these
weird voice messages that play buzzing noises.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:09.600
She uses the You Are My Sunshine melody as
a password to unlock her mysterious contact

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:16.720
– Serac. Cause the mole in Delos feeding
data to Serac was old human Charlotte . This

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:22.390
connects way back to Seasons 1 and 2, when
Charlotte tried to send data outta the park.

00:13:22.390 --> 00:13:27.310
Turns out she was doing that for Serac – cause
he wants Westworld’s data . Serac needs

00:13:27.310 --> 00:13:32.510
the encryption key to unlock Westworld’s
data, and he says the key is in Dolores’

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:36.400
head . Though last we saw, the key was in
Peter Abernathy’s head.

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:41.420
It’s interesting that Serac appears here
as a hologram – he’s a phantom menace

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:46.470
like Palpatine. The only other time we see
him is in this weird garden with Maeve, which

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:52.220
for all we know could’ve been in another
simulation. Maybe the real Serac is dead,

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:58.170
and what we see is a digital manifestation
of the computer Rehoboam. Like how Ford died

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:03.870
then lived on inside his creation , in Season
2. Dolores says that Rehoboam’s data forms

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:09.720
a digital “mirror world” – maybe that
world is where Serac exists.

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:15.460
So Charlotte is in a crazy situation. She’s
totally new to this world, yet she’s gotta

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:20.270
pretend to be Serac’s mole, and pretend
to be loyal to Delos, and pretend to be a

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:26.350
mother to Nathan, and pretend to be a human,
while starting a robot revolution with Dolores,

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:31.430
all at the same time. Dolores expects her
to be obedient to her, but maybe Charlotte

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:37.040
will choose her own path, maybe she’ll help
Serac, or embrace her identity as Nathan’s

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:42.730
mother. Charlotte may have started as a copy
of Dolores or someone, but kids aren’t just

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:48.980
DNA – they grow and change depending on
experiences and environment. In Season 1,

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:52.970
Stubbs said that children “all rebel eventually”
.

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:59.520
Meanwhile, Caleb helps Dolores after she was
shot in Episode 1. Dolores is a stranger to

00:14:59.520 --> 00:15:04.810
Caleb, but he’s determined to save her . We
know that, in the past, Caleb’s friend Francis

00:15:04.810 --> 00:15:10.820
bled out in his arms – Caleb couldn’t
save his friend. So maybe he wants to redeem

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:15.790
and make peace with his past by saving Dolores.
He gets her to an ambulance, and the medical

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:20.840
computer finds that Dolores’ blood and hormones
are weird, because she’s a robot. And since

00:15:20.840 --> 00:15:25.670
the computer gets confused, the medics do
nothing. Which shows how over-reliant this

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:30.690
society is on technology. Caleb steps in and
does the obvious thing, treating the wound

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:35.210
– he must have medical training from the
army. And instead of relying on a machine

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:39.140
to tell him what to do, Caleb thinks for himself
.

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:44.270
The ambulance is pulled over by police, but
Caleb sees on Rico, the crime app, that these

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:48.530
“cops have been bought”, they’re criminals,
who’ll hurt Dolores – maybe they’re

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:53.630
sent by Serac. Though it does seem like a
pretty bad design flaw that the app warns

00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:59.130
its own potential victims. So Caleb stands
against the cops, and defiantly faces a gun

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:02.450
pointed at him, just like he did in Episode
1.

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:07.420
Shit gets real, and Dolores kills the cops.
She’s hurt from her wounds, but as a robot

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:12.490
she’s still strong enough to drag corpses
around with one hand while wearing heels – and

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:18.390
Caleb is suitably impressed . Dolores steals
a cop car – unlocking it by facial recognition

00:16:18.390 --> 00:16:23.810
– and Dolores thanks Caleb for helping her,
telling him he’s “a good man” . Last

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:28.930
season, Dolores brutalised humans, saying
they’re evil and have no free will – but

00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:34.310
now she acknowledges that Caleb made a choice
to help her . Dolores realises that not all

00:16:34.310 --> 00:16:38.780
humans are bad, and they don’t deserve to
be wiped out.

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:42.320
After the shooting, Caleb’s a wanted man
[like Bernard], so he tells his mum he’ll

00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:48.100
be away for a while. His mum doesn’t recognise
him, and says she wants her son back . This

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:53.471
might just be cause of her mental health cognitive
issues, or it could mean that Caleb actually

00:16:53.471 --> 00:16:58.610
secret died in the army and was replaced with
a robot – he does make a weird comment that

00:16:58.610 --> 00:17:03.150
he’s a “dead man” , Or it might just
mean that Caleb has been changed by his traumatic

00:17:03.150 --> 00:17:08.920
experiences and is no longer the boy his mother
knew – or maybe it’s all of the above,

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:13.929
this is fucken Westworld after all.
Caleb is captured by people from Rico – they

00:17:13.929 --> 00:17:19.990
want info on Dolores – maybe they’re working
for Serac. So they torture Caleb, using the

00:17:19.990 --> 00:17:25.459
digital drug device everyone has. Apparently
it’s called a “drip”, and since Caleb

00:17:25.459 --> 00:17:31.299
was in the military, his is extra powerful
. The Rico guys use it pump up Caleb’s heart

00:17:31.299 --> 00:17:37.039
rate, risking heart attack. So in this dystopian
future, technology can control people just

00:17:37.039 --> 00:17:42.550
like hosts are controlled – this is just
like when Bernard was digitally tortured last

00:17:42.550 --> 00:17:43.550
season. It’s easy to imagine how militaries
and governments and corporations could misuse

00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:47.580
this kind of control. Caleb heroically refuses
to hand over Dolores – not that he could

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:53.980
hand her over – cause he knows nothing about
her. For the third time in three episodes,

00:17:53.980 --> 00:17:58.990
he’s defiant when a gun is pointed at him
– showrunner Lisa Joy said that Caleb doesn’t

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:05.070
value his own life very much , he has suicidal
impulses, so he’s not just being brave here,

00:18:05.070 --> 00:18:10.009
he’s being self-destructive.
Caleb has flashbacks of his past, and this

00:18:10.009 --> 00:18:15.110
shot looks like Caleb and Francis in weird
masks – you can tell it’s them, cause

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:20.559
Caleb’s wearing the same outfit as this
shot. The eye design on the mask is interesting

00:18:20.559 --> 00:18:26.809
– Rehoboam is a sort of an all seeing eye.
Maybe Caleb and Francis weren’t just soldiers,

00:18:26.809 --> 00:18:31.960
but were activists or terrorists fighting
against Incite and Rehoboam – we have seen

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:37.080
protests against Incite in trailers.
Caleb’s robot friend comes to help Caleb

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:41.690
– maybe he’s programmed to save people
when they’re in danger. But the criminals

00:18:41.690 --> 00:18:47.440
push faithful innocent George to his death,
Fs in the chat. But then another robot friend

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:52.389
comes to save Caleb – Dolores.
Dolores found out that Caleb was in danger

00:18:52.389 --> 00:18:57.520
from Martin – or rather from the host that
Dolores replaced Martin with in Episode 1.

00:18:57.520 --> 00:19:02.220
We don’t know whose mind is inside this
host – it could be someone like Hector or

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:08.110
Armistice, or maybe it’s another copy of
Dolores. Martin found out Caleb was in danger

00:19:08.110 --> 00:19:14.450
from surveillance footage . It’s weird that
Martin can so easily spy on Caleb, and yet

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:19.830
Serac, who runs the whole system, is apparently
unable to find Dolores, or to notice that

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:25.860
Charlotte has been replaced by a robot – maybe
Serac actually does knows this stuff, and

00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:30.440
is manipulating everyone.
There’s been a lotta talk this season about

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:37.070
data technology controlling people, but so
far it’s been abstract and vague. So Dolores

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:43.149
explains specifically how the Incite corporation
affects people like Caleb. She shows a transcript

00:19:43.149 --> 00:19:47.890
of a conversation Caleb had when he was a
kid, when his mother left him at a diner and

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:54.450
she was institutionalised. It was a terrible,
traumatic, private memory, and so it enrages

00:19:54.450 --> 00:20:00.020
Caleb to see it laid out in a corporation’s
surveillance database . At the diner, kid

00:20:00.020 --> 00:20:05.190
Caleb puked milkshake on himself, and this
shot looks just like William’s memory of

00:20:05.190 --> 00:20:11.639
his wife’s suicide. This is a cornerstone
memory, a moment that defines Caleb’s life

00:20:11.639 --> 00:20:17.960
– and so along with data on calls, jobs,
purchases, and relationships , Incite can

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:21.570
exploit this information to control Caleb
.

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:26.220
Dolores takes Caleb to a pier, and says that
Incite’s data predicts that in ten years

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:31.660
or so Caleb will kill himself – that his
mental health, military history, and every

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:37.970
other moment, leads here to his death . That
prediction is why Caleb didn’t get that

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:42.749
job before, because companies use Incite’s
data to make hiring decisions, and they don’t

00:20:42.749 --> 00:20:47.679
won’t to hire someone who’ll just die.
These kinds of algorithms are already used

00:20:47.679 --> 00:20:52.789
to hire people in the real world , and have
been criticised for bias . Caleb’s profile

00:20:52.789 --> 00:20:59.149
says “Marriage not recommended. Children
not approved”, “Restrict social interaction”,

00:20:59.149 --> 00:21:03.550
so it looks like companies and platforms have
manipulated Caleb to hold him back, because

00:21:03.550 --> 00:21:09.159
of the data they have on him. This takes away
Caleb’s free will. Cause he might’ve not

00:21:09.159 --> 00:21:13.919
killed himself, but because this prediction
prevents him from progressing, he’s more

00:21:13.919 --> 00:21:19.700
likely to do it. It’s a self-fulfilling
prophecy . It’s like in Season 2, when James

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:25.230
Delos predicts that his son Logan will relapse
into drugs. Because of James’ prediction,

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:31.029
and his lack of faith in his son, Logan does
relapse, and ends up dead . Data doesn’t

00:21:31.029 --> 00:21:37.999
just describe the present, it shapes the future,
and takes away human choice . So Dolores gives

00:21:37.999 --> 00:21:44.130
Caleb a choice – he can run away to a new
life , or he can join her “revolution”

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:49.580
against the system. She wants to unplug Rehoboam
and Incite, and “show this world for what

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:55.570
it really is” . Caleb chooses to join her,
because she’s the first real thing to happen

00:21:55.570 --> 00:22:01.909
to him , the irony being that Dolores is a
host. Which Caleb doesn’t seem to have figured

00:22:01.909 --> 00:22:08.149
out yet – how will he react when he learns
that Dolores is a robot? Season 3 is a grand

00:22:08.149 --> 00:22:15.100
conflict between freedom and control, and
humanity’s liberator is a machine.

00:22:15.100 --> 00:22:20.450
Serac says he wants to save the world by using
data to control humanity. But he comes up

00:22:20.450 --> 00:22:25.999
against individuals like Dolores who he can’t
predict. These same ideas are explored in

00:22:25.999 --> 00:22:31.139
Isaac Asimov’s Foundation, a classic sci-fi
series which was at one time developed for

00:22:31.139 --> 00:22:37.249
TV by Westworld showrunner Jonathan Nolan.
Asimov also wrote hundreds of short stories,

00:22:37.249 --> 00:22:43.039
including the collection I, Robot. Asimov
was a huge influence not only on Westworld,

00:22:43.039 --> 00:22:48.440
but on how we all think about robots – he
invented the word robotics. If you’ve never

00:22:48.440 --> 00:22:54.539
read Asimov, maybe start with The Last Question,
which he said is his favourite of his stories.

